  "body": "## What \u0026 why\n\nOn a 4K@144 DisplayPort link with DSC + VRR, the monitor briefly blanks / re-syncs\n(\"flash\") on alt-tab to/from the app — and only this app triggers it. Root cause:\nthe app's video surface (borderless, client-filling, opaque, flip-model) is the only\nsurface on the machine eligible for a DWM hardware-overlay / **independent-flip** plane,\nso DWM promotes it on focus-gain and demotes it on focus-loss. That per-focus-edge\nscanout-plane retopology re-trains the DSC/VRR display link → the flash.\n\n**Fix:** a sub-unity DirectComposition opacity effect (0.99) on the video visual forces\nDWM to alpha-blend it, which is inexpressible as an MPO overlay (no constant-alpha plane\nmode) — so the plane is pinned to `Composed: Flip`. No promotion churn, no re-train.\n\n## Evidence (PresentMon, `PresentMode` column)\n\n| | foreground present mode |\n|---|---|\n| Before | predominantly `Hardware Composed: Independent Flip` |\n| After | **592/592** `Composed: Flip` (foreground); **1104/1104**, 0 transitions across a 45s real-use alt-tab capture |\n\nThe churn is eliminated at the objective layer. The physical flash has not recurred in\ntesting, but the symptom is intermittent, so long-run real-use confirmation is ongoing.\nMechanism confidence ~0.65 (the final causal link — plane retopology *alone* re-training\nthe link — is inferred, not documented end-to-end).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `compositor.rs`: occlusion/minimize standby for the render pump; force-composed video plane (the flash fix). Net `+46/-2`.\n- `docs/adr/0002-force-composed-video-plane.md`: the decision record, incl. rejected alternatives.\n- `docs/feature-contracts/desktop-shell.md`: render-policy note on the forced composition.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- **SDR-coupled:** forcing composition also defeats HDR passthrough. Inert today (8-bit SDR swapchain), but the effect must be gated off if HDR is ever enabled. Documented in ADR-0002.\n- Video loses the independent-flip fast path (minor power/GPU cost) — the deliberate trade.\n\n## Note for the merger\n\nHistory includes `2189a91 DIAGNOSTIC (do not merge)` and a focus-gating experiment that\nwas reverted; they cancel out in the tree. **Squash-merge recommended** to keep `main` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
